People ask about that store a lot. It depended on where you were standing. About thirty-five people sheltered in the training room at the back, and if you were in there, the concrete walls fell outward, away from you. Out in the rest of the store, eight people were lost. The store's managers said they'd just come in through the lumber entrance and were walking along the front wall when it came down. The tornado's center passed between those two stores, and very near a Pizza Hut. What did the people inside it do when the siren went again?